sources=[{'id':i,'title':t,'url':u} for i,t,u in source_rows]
schedule='Take alectinib twice daily with food, every day, with no planned rest week. After surgery, treatment lasts up to 24 months, stopping sooner for recurrence or unacceptable side effects. For advanced cancer, treatment continues until progression or unacceptable side effects under the oncology plan.'
admin='The usual starting dose is 600 mg twice daily: four 150 mg capsules each time, taken with food. Use your own prescription, which may specify a lower dose. Swallow capsules whole; do not open or dissolve them.'
missed='If a dose is missed, take it only if the next dose is more than 6 hours away. If the next dose is due within 6 hours, skip the missed dose. Do not take two doses together. If you vomit after a dose, take the next dose at its usual time; do not take an extra dose.'
scope='This guide covers alectinib alone for ALK-positive lung cancer. Confirm whether it is adjuvant treatment after complete surgery, first treatment for advanced cancer, or treatment after crizotinib. These settings have different evidence and treatment lengths.'
purpose='Alectinib targets an abnormal ALK growth signal. After complete surgery the aim is to reduce the chance of cancer returning; in advanced cancer the aim is to control the cancer. Your team explains the individual aim, alternatives and uncertainty.'
baseline=['Confirm ALK-positive NSCLC by a validated test; establish indication, staging/resection and prior-treatment history.','FBC, renal and liver profile, CPK, blood pressure and ECG before treatment.','Review all medicines, supplements, muscle/lung/cardiac symptoms, pregnancy, contraception and breastfeeding.','For treatment after crizotinib allow a minimum 7-day washout. For adjuvant treatment confirm complete resection, high-risk criteria and ECOG 0–1.']
ongoing=['Liver profile every 2 weeks for the first 3 months, then every 4 weeks or as clinically indicated.','FBC and renal profile every 4 weeks. CPK every 2 weeks for the first month, then as clinically indicated, including muscle symptoms.','Blood pressure and pulse as clinically indicated. NCCP says ECG prior to cycle 2, then as indicated; a continuous oral regimen has no defined cycle length, so agree the first repeat ECG appointment locally.','Assess symptoms, interactions, adherence, current dose and treatment benefit; scans and disease monitoring follow the Consultant plan.']
urgent='Contact the oncology team promptly for new or worsening cough or breathlessness, unexplained muscle pain or weakness, yellow skin or eyes, dark urine, marked tiredness or pallor, dizziness or fainting, severe abdominal pain, persistent vomiting or diarrhoea, or reduced urine. Sudden serious breathing difficulty, severe chest pain or collapse needs emergency help. Do not wait for the next blood test.'
mechanism='Alectinib blocks the abnormal ALK protein that drives growth in ALK-positive cancer cells. It can act against cancer in the body and brain. It can also affect healthy tissues, so blood tests and symptom checks remain important.'
risks=['Muscle pain or weakness and raised CPK','Liver injury and raised liver tests or bilirubin','Anaemia, including destruction of red blood cells (haemolysis)','Slow heart rate, dizziness or fainting','Lung inflammation (ILD/pneumonitis), which can be serious','Constipation, nausea, diarrhoea and swelling','Skin rash and sensitivity to sunlight','Gastrointestinal perforation; urgent severe abdominal pain','Potential harm to a developing baby']
limits=['ALINA studied completely resected stage IB (tumour ≥4 cm)–IIIA disease using AJCC/UICC 7th edition. Modern stage labels require mapping, not automatic substitution.','ALINA compared 24 months of alectinib with four cycles of platinum chemotherapy; it did not test routinely adding alectinib after adjuvant chemotherapy.','ALINA 2025 updated disease-free results are a conference analysis with 8 December 2024 efficacy cutoff; overall survival remained immature. Do not translate DFS into proven survival or individual cure estimates.','ALEX studied untreated advanced disease against crizotinib, not other modern ALK inhibitors. Final OS HR 0.78 (95% CI 0.56–1.08) did not establish a statistically significant OS difference.','Ou phase II was a single-arm post-crizotinib study, mostly previously chemotherapy-treated; response rates do not establish comparative survival benefit.','NCCP 00401c lists reimbursement N/A. NCCP indication, EMA licence, trial population and current access/reimbursement are separate facts.','Software source checks do not constitute independent clinical, pharmacy or patient/PPI approval.']
evidence_text='After complete surgery, ALINA found that alectinib delayed cancer recurrence compared with platinum chemotherapy; whether it improves overall survival remains uncertain. In untreated advanced cancer, ALEX showed better cancer control than crizotinib, but its final survival comparison did not establish a clear overall-survival difference. Separate studies showed tumour responses after crizotinib. These groups cannot predict your personal outcome or rank all current treatment choices.'
def item(title,text,ids=['nccp','smpc']):return {'title':title,'text':text,'source_ids':ids}
support=[item('Anti-sickness medicines','Alectinib is minimal-to-low oral emetic risk. Treat nausea with prescribed as-required medicine if needed. Routine preventive anti-sickness treatment and infusion premedication are not required; your team selects a suitable rescue medicine.',['nccp','oral-antiemetic','antiemetic']),item('Capsules, food and missed doses',admin+' '+missed),item('Muscles, liver, blood and breathing','Keep liver, CPK and blood-count appointments. Muscle symptoms, jaundice, dark urine, unusual fatigue, cough or breathlessness need prompt review even between appointments.'),item('Heart rate and other medicines','Tell the team about dizziness, fainting and medicines that slow the pulse. Check new prescriptions, supplements, grapefruit and Seville oranges with pharmacy; interactions may require closer monitoring rather than an automatic dose change.'),item('Sun protection','Avoid prolonged sunlight during treatment and for at least 7 days after stopping. Use broad-spectrum UVA/UVB sunscreen and lip balm SPF 50 or higher.',['smpc']),item('Pregnancy, contraception and breastfeeding','Women who could become pregnant need highly effective contraception during treatment and for at least 5 weeks afterwards. Men with female partners who could become pregnant need highly effective contraception during treatment and for at least 3 months afterwards. Oral contraceptive effectiveness may be reduced: ask for a suitable method. Do not breastfeed during treatment. Discuss fertility before treatment and contact the team promptly if pregnancy occurs.',['smpc'])]
columns=['Before starting','First month','Months 2–3','From month 4','Completion / change']
monitorrows=[{'label':'Alectinib','cells':['Confirm setting and prescription','Twice daily with food','Continue daily if authorised','Continue with review','Adjuvant maximum 24 months; advanced duration depends on benefit/toxicity']},{'label':'Liver tests','cells':['Baseline liver profile','Every 2 weeks','Every 2 weeks','Every 4 weeks or as needed','Follow unresolved abnormalities']},{'label':'CPK / muscles','cells':['Baseline CPK','Every 2 weeks','As clinically indicated','As clinically indicated','Check recovery if held']},{'label':'Blood count / kidneys','cells':['Baseline FBC and renal profile','Every 4 weeks','Every 4 weeks','Every 4 weeks','Follow anaemia and renal concerns']},{'label':'Pulse / blood pressure / ECG','cells':['Baseline BP and ECG','Agree early repeat ECG timing','Pulse/BP and ECG as needed','Repeat as clinically indicated','Confirm recovery and medicine review']},{'label':'Cancer and symptoms','cells':['Confirm aim and disease assessment','Report new symptoms promptly','Review tolerability and adherence','Imaging per Consultant plan','Agree follow-up or next treatment']}]
patient={'schema_version':1,'content_version':V,'suite_release':V,'service_kind':'targeted','review_status':STATUS,'source_checked':DATE,'protocol_id':p['protocol_id'],'code':'00401','protocol_version':'6','title':'Alectinib monotherapy','cycle_days':None,'schedule_kind':'continuous_oral','schedule_label':'Continuous twice-daily capsules','cycle_display':'Continuous daily treatment','therapy_label':'ALK-targeted oral treatment','context_label':'ALK-positive NSCLC · adjuvant or advanced disease','scope_heading':'Confirm your alectinib treatment setting','scope_note':scope,'indication_text':purpose,'purpose':purpose,'schedule_summary':schedule,'administration_text':admin+' '+missed,'monitoring_summary':' '.join(ongoing),'sources':sources,'agents':[{'id':'alectinib','name':'Alectinib','alias':'Alecensa','type':'ALK inhibitor','mechanism':'Blocks an abnormal ALK growth signal','explanation':mechanism,'visual':['ALK signal drives cancer growth','Alectinib blocks ALK activity','Growth can slow or stop'],'watch':'Take with food. Keep blood tests and report muscle weakness, breathing changes, jaundice or dizziness promptly.','source_ids':['nccp','smpc'],'risks':risks,'symptoms':['Muscle pain / weakness','Breathlessness / cough','Dizziness / fainting','Constipation','Fatigue','Skin / sunlight changes']}],'timeline_source_ids':['nccp','smpc'],'support_source_ids':['nccp','smpc','oral-antiemetic','antiemetic'],'urgent_source_ids':['smpc'],'phases_title':'Continuous treatment with a setting-specific endpoint','phases_note':schedule,'medicines_title':'Your targeted medicine','timeline_note':'Relative timing only. Symptoms can occur at any time; no dates or personal information are required.','safety_note':'Keep your oncology emergency number available. A serious symptom needs review between scheduled visits.','urgent_extra':urgent,'teachback':'Can you explain your treatment aim and duration, how to take capsules with food, what to do after a missed or vomited dose, and which symptoms need urgent contact?','consent_support':'Discuss the individual aim, the evidence for your setting, alternatives including not proceeding, uncertainty, material risks, pregnancy/fertility, daily capsules, monitoring and access. You can ask for an interpreter, more time or another explanation and can reconsider. This aid supports a consent conversation; it does not replace it.','phases':[{'id':'continuous_oral','label':'Daily alectinib','short':'Twice daily with food','cycles':[],'agents':['alectinib'],'detail':schedule}],'timeline':[],'day_groups':[],'chronology_notes':[{'title':'Early checks','text':'Liver tests every 2 weeks for 3 months; CPK every 2 weeks for the first month.'},{'title':'Continuous dosing','text':schedule},{'title':'ECG timing','text':'Ask when the first repeat ECG is booked. NCCP uses the phrase prior to cycle 2 without defining an oral cycle length.'}],'support':support,'port_pump':False,'longitudinal_mapping':True,'passport_visit_note':'Use the passport for ongoing oral treatment reviews. The number of recording pages is not a prescribed duration. Record dose changes, missed doses and symptoms; do not use it to authorise your own dose.','anatomy_note':'Possible effects do not predict what will happen to you. Symptoms can have other causes and need assessment.','anatomy':[['lung','New cough or breathlessness','alectinib','Report promptly because lung inflammation can occur.',59,28],['heart','Dizziness or fainting','alectinib','A slow pulse can be symptomatic and needs medicine review.',43,30],['liver','Liver tests / jaundice','alectinib','Liver injury may start silently; keep tests and report yellow skin or dark urine.',42,42],['blood','Fatigue or pallor','alectinib','Anaemia can include red-cell breakdown; report marked changes.',62,45],['muscle','Muscle pain or weakness','alectinib','CPK tests help assess muscle injury; report unexplained symptoms.',33,64],['skin','Sun sensitivity','alectinib','Use high-factor sun protection during treatment and for 7 days after stopping.',65,64]],'monitoring_schedule':{'title':'Treatment and monitoring over time','columns':columns,'rows':monitorrows,'note':'Intervals are reference guidance, not booked appointments. Ask who arranges tests, reviews results and authorises treatment.','source_ids':['nccp','smpc']},'logistics':{'nav_label':'Capsules and visits','title':'Your practical treatment plan','intro':schedule,'sections':[{'title':'Before starting','text':'Confirm ALK result, treatment setting, dose, baseline tests and access. After crizotinib the team allows at least 7 days before alectinib.'},{'title':'Taking capsules','text':admin},{'title':'Missed or vomited dose','text':missed},{'title':'Supply and visits','text':'Request the next supply before capsules run out. Blood tests and ECGs need their own appointments. Alectinib itself does not require a line or infusion pump.'},{'title':'A hold or dose change','text':'Ask what is held, what needs to recover and who will authorise restarting. Do not restart or change the dose yourself.'},{'title':'Completion or change','text':schedule}]},'evidence':{'title':'Evidence differs after surgery and in advanced cancer','intro':'Studies describe groups in a particular setting. Ask which comparison applies to you.','population':'Completely resected ALK-positive NSCLC; untreated advanced ALK-positive NSCLC; or advanced cancer after crizotinib, studied separately.','interpretation':evidence_text,'limitations':'The after-surgery study does not yet establish a survival benefit. Advanced-disease trials do not compare every modern ALK medicine. Group averages do not predict an individual result.','metrics':[],'source_ids':['alina','alina-update','alex-final','ou-phase2']}}
patient['endocrine_timeline']={'title':'Capsules, checks and next decisions','intro':'No dates or personal information are needed. Columns show sequence, not equal periods.','columns':columns,'rows':[{'label':'Start safely','kind':'checks','start':1,'end':1,'text':'Confirm ALK result, treatment setting, prescription, baseline tests and prior-crizotinib washout.'},{'label':'Active treatment','kind':'treatment','start':2,'end':4,'text':'Alectinib twice daily with food, with no planned rest week.'},{'label':'Liver monitoring','kind':'checks','start':2,'end':4,'text':'Every 2 weeks for 3 months; then every 4 weeks or as needed.'},{'label':'Muscles, blood and heart','kind':'checks','start':2,'end':4,'text':'Early CPK checks; 4-week blood count/kidney tests; pulse/BP and agreed ECG review.'},{'label':'Completion or change','kind':'checks','start':5,'end':5,'text':'Adjuvant maximum 24 months; advanced treatment until progression or unacceptable toxicity.'}],'notes':[missed,'Keep reporting symptoms between visits. An agreed treatment hold takes priority over the daily schedule.']}
patient['chapters']=[{'id':'treatment-purpose','title':'Understanding your treatment','intro':scope,'items':[item('Your treatment aim',purpose),item('How long treatment lasts',schedule),item('Evidence for your setting',evidence_text,['alina','alina-update','alex-final','ou-phase2'])]},{'id':'starting','title':'Before the first capsules','intro':'Confirm a practical plan with your team.','items':[item('Baseline checks',' '.join(baseline)),item('Oral treatment and access','Confirm the prescription and supply route. Adjuvant use is listed in NCCP, but the printed reimbursement field is N/A; the team checks current access separately.') ]},{'id':'taking-capsules','title':'Taking alectinib','intro':admin,'items':[item('Missed or vomited dose',missed),item('Medicines and food','Check all prescribed, over-the-counter and herbal products with pharmacy. Ask specifically about medicines that slow the pulse and grapefruit/Seville oranges. Do not stop another prescribed medicine on your own.',['smpc'])]},{'id':'tests-and-symptoms','title':'Tests and symptom review','intro':'Blood-test results may change without symptoms.','items':[item('Scheduled monitoring',' '.join(ongoing)),item('Symptoms between visits',urgent,['smpc'])]},{'id':'daily-living','title':'Daily living and planning','intro':'Raise practical concerns early.','items':[support[4],support[5],item('Future treatment decisions','Discuss benefit, side effects and priorities at reviews. After planned adjuvant completion, agree the ongoing lung-cancer follow-up plan.')]}]
patient['questions']=[{'q':'Does taking capsules mean fewer important risks?','a':'Capsules are cancer treatment and can cause serious side effects. Keep the planned tests and use the oncology contact plan for new symptoms.'},{'q':'Does having side effects show it is working?','a':'No. Side effects do not reliably indicate cancer response; your team assesses benefit using the relevant follow-up plan.'},{'q':'How long will I take alectinib?','a':schedule},{'q':'What if I miss a dose or vomit?','a':missed},{'q':'Which blood tests happen early?','a':'Liver tests are planned every 2 weeks for 3 months. CPK is checked every 2 weeks for the first month. Blood count and kidney tests are checked every 4 weeks; symptoms may prompt extra tests.'},{'q':'When is my next ECG?','a':'NCCP asks for an ECG before its second treatment cycle, but this medicine is taken continuously. Ask the team to confirm the first repeat ECG appointment and later checks.'},{'q':'Can I change or restart my dose myself?','a':'No. If alectinib is held or reduced, ask what needs to recover, when review happens and who will authorise restarting.'},{'q':'What should I say when calling?','a':'Give the medicine name, current dose, last dose, symptoms and when they began. Explain whether you can drink, pass urine and manage usual activities. Do not delay calling to collect details.'},{'q':'Can I use this page to decide whether tests are safe?','a':'No. Blood results, symptoms, current dose and treatment history need the prescriber’s assessment. This guide does not authorise treatment.'},{'q':'Do I need to enter dates?','a':'No. This map shows general timing. Your hospital arranges actual appointments.'}]
clinical={'component_rationale':mechanism,'key_points':['Separate 00401a post-crizotinib, 00401b first-line advanced and 00401c adjuvant after complete resection.','600 mg twice daily with food continuously; reduction levels 450 then 300 mg twice daily; discontinue if 300 mg twice daily cannot be tolerated.','Adjuvant maximum 24 months; advanced until progression or unacceptable toxicity. Minimum 7-day crizotinib washout for 00401a.','ILD at any grade needs interruption; permanent discontinuation requires no other potential cause.','CPK >5 versus >10 ×ULN and recurrence have different restart pathways. Haemolysis needs haemoglobin and diagnostic context.','Combined liver-test permanent-stop rule requires exclusion of cholestasis/haemolysis.','Bradycardia grade, contributing medicine adjustment and recurrence determine restart/stop advice; no imported QTcF cutoff.','NCCP and current SmPC support Child-Pugh C starting dose 450 mg twice daily; severe renal impairment/dialysis does not automatically require a reduction.'], 'patient_selection':{'treatment_intent':purpose,'disease_and_biomarker_context':[x['description'] for x in p['indications']],'eligibility_orientation':baseline,'important_cautions':limits},'support_summary':[x['text'] for x in support],'baseline':baseline,'before_each_cycle':['Continuous oral treatment: no invented cycle interval. At each review check symptoms, adherence, current dose, interactions and the time-based monitoring plan.'],'ongoing':ongoing,'administration':[admin,missed],'access':['Oral capsules; no routine infusion line or pump.','Confirm local dispensing/access separately for each indication.'],'rationale':{'summary':purpose,'setting':'ALK-positive NSCLC; adjuvant or advanced, separated by indication','line':'Adjuvant after complete resection, first-line advanced, or advanced after crizotinib.','factors':['Validated ALK result, disease stage/resection, prior therapy, organ function, current symptoms, medicine interactions and patient priorities.'],'alternatives':['Discuss contemporary ALK-directed options, surgery/adjuvant strategy where appropriate, clinical trials, supportive care and not proceeding with the MDT.'],'limitations':limits,'sources':[{'label':t,'url':u} for i,t,u in source_rows if i in ['alina','alina-update','alex-final','ou-phase2']]}}
